! h3-chain-lsda-fixed.in doubled along z: two hydrogen trimers a cell, the
! same spacings (1.6, 1.8 and 2.0 bohr), the chains 7 bohr apart, held at two
! Bohr magnetons a cell by fixed occupations, both trimers polarized the same
! way. Its zone-centre phonon is the primitive cell's at q = 0 and at
! q = b3/2 together (I82). The 1x1x4 grid is the exact folding of the
! primitive 1x1x8: the doubled cell's b3 is half the primitive's.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, nat = 6, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    nspin = 2
    occupations = 'fixed'
    tot_magnetization = 2
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.3
    nosym = .true.
    noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.4
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
CELL_PARAMETERS bohr
 7.0 0.0 0.0
 0.0 7.0 0.0
 0.0 0.0 10.8
ATOMIC_POSITIONS bohr
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
 H 0.0 0.0 1.6
 H 0.0 0.0 3.4
 H 0.0 0.0 5.4
 H 0.0 0.0 7.0
 H 0.0 0.0 8.8
K_POINTS (automatic)
 1 1 4 0 0 0
